@namespace FormCraft.ForFluentUI

@* The visible required marker for a file-upload field's own label (#262, #278).

   Lives here rather than inline in each upload component so the single- and multiple-file
   components cannot drift — markup divergence between two copies of the same thing is the failure
   class this library keeps re-filing (#146, #177, #184, #189).

   aria-hidden: the requirement is conveyed programmatically by the browse control's
   aria-describedby, so announcing "star" here would only duplicate it.

   `formcraft-required-marker` is FormCraft's own hook and the class to select or restyle. The
   asterisk is a real text node, not CSS `content` — nothing in Fluent's stylesheet draws a required
   marker for this markup, so there is no framework rule to override. *@

<span class="formcraft-required-marker" aria-hidden="true" data-testid="formcraft-upload-required-marker">&nbsp;*</span>
